    <Label IsHitTestVisible="false" Name="Description" Style="GalleryText" Text="Every triangle has exactly one circle through\nall three vertices: its circumcircle.\n\nThe gray points are the midpoints of the\nsides, and the gray lines are the\nperpendicular bisectors. They always meet in\none point, the circumcenter - the center of\nthe circle.\n\nDrag the yellow vertices. When does the center\nleave the triangle?" DecimalsToShow="2" X="6.695" Y="7.64" />
